{"content":[{"c":["MEHOLAH, MEHOLATHITE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Location used to describe Adriel the son of Barzillai, who was the husband of Merab, Saul’s eldest daughter (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.18.19","r":"1Sam.18.19","rawR":"1Sam.18.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.18.19","value":"1Sam.18.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 18:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.8","r":"2Sam.21.8","rawR":"2Sam.21.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.8","value":"2Sam.21.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 21:8"},"). He was probably from Abel-meholah, an important city of Gilead. The marriage of Adriel and Merab was probably a political move by Saul, agreed to by David, who was to have married Merab himself (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.18.17-19","r":"1Sam.18.17-19","rawR":"1Sam.18.17-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.18.17-19","value":"1Sam.18.17-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 18:17-19"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MeholahMeholathite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 18:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.18.19","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.18.19","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.18.19"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 21:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.21.8","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.21.8","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.21.8"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 18:17-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.18.17-19","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.18.17-19","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.18.17-19"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5407bbdb86b4d10d0898447d4ce61fe1068986a3c7709db36c20625a57c98920","sourceItemName":"MeholahMeholathite","sourceItemOrder":213,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"MeholahMeholathite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact